course: dictionary
lesson: 8890
title: Shrewd: clever and careful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shrewd person is clever at seeing what is really going on. They notice tricks, think ahead and make sensible choices, especially about money. A shrewd shopkeeper or detective is hard to fool.
explain: Look at the context for clues. «You can forgive fully and still be careful: be as shrewd as snakes and as innocent as doves» tells you shrewd is a good quality, the opposite of being silly or easily tricked. Ask yourself: would a clever, careful person fit here? Yes, so shrewd means clever and careful.
explain: Shrewd can also describe a guess or a choice. A «shrewd guess» is a wise guess that is likely to be right. A «shrewd move» is a clever, practical step. Shrewd is mostly praise, but it can hint that someone is a little sly, so check the rest of the story to see how it is used.
fact: Shrewd means clever at understanding people and situations.
fact: Shrewd can describe a person, a guess, a choice or a move.
fact: «A shrewd businesswoman» is a clever woman who makes good decisions about money or business.
fact: The adverb is shrewdly, and the comparative forms are shrewder and shrewdest.
fact: A shrewd guess is wise and likely to be right.
exercise: «As shrewd as snakes and as innocent as doves» means being as shrewd as snakes. What does shrewd mean here? | Silly and careless | *Clever and careful | Slow and sleepy | Loud and cheerful
exercise: A shopper compares prices and finds the best deal every time. Which word describes her? | *Shrewd | Sleepy | Shy | Shaky
exercise: Which word is the adverb form of shrewd? | *shrewdly | shrew | shrewdest | shrewder
test: A «shrewd guess» is a guess that is likely to be... | *Right | Long | Loud | Silly
test: Which person is the most shrewd? | A dog who sleeps all day | A man who never thinks ahead | *A detective who spots the trick at once | A child who believes every trick
exam: Which sentence uses shrewd correctly? | The shrewd rain fell all day. | *The shrewd shopkeeper spotted the fake coin. | The soup was shrewd and warm. | He shrewd his bed at night.
